@startuml

title PENA POC 01 — LLM Summarization Design

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor #2F5597
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FBFF
  ParticipantBorderColor #2F5597
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FBFF
}

participant "Runtime Pipeline" as PIPE
participant "Context Loader" as CTX
participant "Prompt Builder" as PROMPT
participant "LLM Client" as CLIENT
participant "LLM Provider" as LLM
participant "Summary Parser" as PARSER
participant "Summary Validator" as VALIDATOR
participant "Observability Writer" as OBS

database "Repository Context\nSpecs / Prompts / Preferences" as REPO
database "Summary Result" as RESULT

PIPE -> CTX : request grounding context
CTX -> REPO : load trusted context\nsummary instructions\nprompt template
REPO --> CTX : context package
CTX --> PIPE : grounding context

PIPE -> PROMPT : build prompt(article, context)
PROMPT --> PIPE : structured prompt

PIPE -> CLIENT : summarize(prompt, model_config)
CLIENT -> LLM : call model
LLM --> CLIENT : raw response
CLIENT --> PIPE : model response

PIPE -> PARSER : parse structured response
PARSER --> PIPE : parsed summary object

PIPE -> VALIDATOR : validate schema\nrequired fields\nuncertainty notes

alt valid response
  VALIDATOR --> PIPE : accepted summary
  PIPE -> RESULT : store summary result
else invalid response
  VALIDATOR --> PIPE : validation error
  PIPE -> OBS : record parse/validation failure
end

PIPE -> OBS : record prompt version\nmodel used\nlatency\nsummary metadata

note over PROMPT,CLIENT
The LLM call must be grounded by:
- article content
- repository context
- prompt template
- output constraints
end note

note over VALIDATOR,OBS
POC 01 should validate structure first.
Do not over-test subjective summary quality yet.
end note

@enduml
